    "scripts.import.demo.text" : {
      "comment" : "Pre-filled mock text loaded into the bulk-import editor when the user opens it for the first time. Mimics what a creator would paste from a notes app — three short Reel ideas separated by numbered headings. Shown only in the demo onboarding pass; the real (Pro) flow opens with an empty editor and the user pastes their own document.",
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Reel ideas this week\n\n1. Why your videos look robotic\nYou read off-camera. Viewers see your eyes drift away. Trust drops. Cut to side-by-side: eye contact vs not. Hook: stop looking like a robot. End: your eyes belong on the lens.\n\n2. The one-take trick\nMemorizing scripts wastes hours. Three takes minimum. Then editing. Show clock. Show stack of failed takes. Then SteadyEye. One take. Done.\n\n3. What I learned from 100 Reels\nMost creators record five takes or more. Pro creators record one. The difference: they don't memorize. They use prompters. But not the scrolling kind."
          }
        }
      }
    },
